 ],
 "notes": "36 stations in a single-column list, lines 1518-1553. The list has no sub-headings, so coast is the section heading, 'East Coast of England'. Fragments are copied exactly, with the spacing between the name and keeper columns kept and only the two-space indent at the start of each line dropped. Each keeper is copied without the full stop that ends the row. Where two keepers are joined by 'and', I split them into two entries; none of them uses 'Messrs'.\n\nNot printed in this list: map numbers, marks for stations that sent returns, and light characters. Those fields are null in every row.\n\nCounts: the text just before the list (lines 1510-1511) says schedules went to 45 stations and 42 sent returns. Only 36 are listed here and 4 are marked _Nil._, so the list doesn't match those numbers.\n\nSpellings copied as printed, which a reader may want to check:\n- 'Llyn Wells' is presumably the Lynn Well light-vessel.\n- 'Languard Point' is presumably Landguard Point.\n- 'Hasbro'' is Happisburgh.\n- 'Farn' stays as printed for Farne.\n- 'Orfordness' is printed as one word.\n\nName choices:\n- In 'Tees, 5 Buoy L.V.' I treated '5 Buoy' as part of the name, not a committee map number.\n- In 'Whitby High L.H.' I kept 'High' as part of the name.\n- 'Leman and Ower L.V.' is one light-vessel, not two stations.\n\nGeography: Hanois L.H. is off Guernsey in the Channel Islands, not on the East Coast, but it is printed in this list and I kept it here.\n\nSame name, different station: Spurn and Hasbro' each appear twice, once as L.H. and once as L.V. These are separate stations.\n\nKeepers to check:\n- 'I. H. Johnson' (Corton) may be a misreading of 'J. H.'; copied as printed.\n- 'Edward le Gallais' has a lower-case 'le', as printed.\n- 'Charles Perfrement' is copied as printed.\n\nAfter the list, lines 1555 onward give 'Reports and notes have also been received from', a list of private observers, not stations. It is outside the requested range and I left it out.",
